  "facts": [
    "Bugrinsky Bridge, opened by President Vladimir Putin on 8 October 2014, became Novosibirsk's third Ob River crossing, replacing the outdated Olovozavodskoy name with a nod to the nearby Bugrinskaya grove.",
    "Spanning 2,091 meters with a 70‑meter-high arch, the Bugrinsky Bridge’s central span stretches 380 meters, accommodating six traffic lanes and earning a 2016 FIDIC Award of Merit for innovation and sustainability.",
    "Construction kicked off in February 2010 and wrapped up in October 2014, a four‑year effort that culminated in a landmark bridge named by a unanimous commission on 3 December 2013."
